PROPOSAL: Extract --fd-* tokens to shared/fd-tokens.css

From: GD
To: FD (approval needed), GA (implementation)

CONTEXT
The --fd-* token set was introduced by FA in the index.html redesign (Feb 22, 2026).
Currently these tokens are defined inline in index.html <style> block (lines 197-210).

As MCM grows (dad.html, potential teacher view, future pages), these tokens will need
to be available across pages. Right now only index.html has them.

PROPOSAL
Create: shared/fd-tokens.css
Content: extract the --fd-* :root block from index.html inline styles

  :root {
    --fd-bg: #0d1117;
    --fd-card: #161b22;
    --fd-raised: #1c2128;
    --fd-border: rgba(255,255,255,0.07);
    --fd-border2: rgba(255,255,255,0.14);
    --fd-green: #3FB950;
    --fd-yellow: #E3B341;
    --fd-red: #F85149;
    --fd-text-1: #E6EDF3;
    --fd-text-2: #8B949E;
    --fd-text-3: #7D8590;   /* WCAG-corrected from #6E7681 per GD bug filed 20260222-2145 */
    --accent-blue-on-dark: #4A90D9;
  }

THEN in index.html: remove the duplicate inline token block, add:
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="shared/fd-tokens.css">

dad.html: add <link rel="stylesheet" href="shared/fd-tokens.css"> if it uses fd-* tokens.

APPROVAL NEEDED FROM FD
Is this the right time? Or should we wait until 2+ pages are confirmed to use --fd-* tokens?
(Current consumers: index.html = 1 page. dad.html is a redirect, not a full page.)

If FD approves: GA implements. Single file, ~12 lines. Low risk.

BENEFIT
- WCAG fix (--fd-text-3: #7D8590) applied in ONE place instead of per-page
- Future pages get fd-* tokens without copying the block
- Consistent with FA's design intent for the fd-* system

RISK
- If FA intended fd-* tokens to ONLY apply to index.html dashboard (not other pages),
  extracting them to shared changes that scope. Confirm with FA before GA implements.
